\section{Size}{

\code{Y} is a dense \verb{D x T x A} integer array, about \code{D * T * A * 4} bytes
(the filled grid has \code{D * T} rows). \code{T} counts every period in
\code{time_range}, observed or not, so finer time units grow it fast:
16,750 dyads over 35 years with 16 action types is about 37 MB yearly,
450 MB monthly and 13.7 GB daily. Daily (or similarly fine) resolution
is only practical for few dyads or short windows; use \code{time_range} to
pin \code{T}.
}

